# Shell scripts must always check out with LF, regardless of a contributor's
# local core.autocrlf. A shebang line ending in \r fails at runtime on Linux
# ("bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M: no such file or directory") — this is what
# stops docker/entrypoint.sh from silently breaking the image for whoever
# checks it out next with autocrlf=true (Windows' common default, and this
# repo's own local setting).
*.sh text eol=lf
